    "table-2-b8e62447": {
      "id": "table-2-b8e62447",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Command",
          "Description"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "/status",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Show conversation state"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "/reset",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "Start fresh: clears the AI session, releases the execution binding (working-directory override + isolation env), and abandons this conversation's "
              },
              {
                "insert": "resumable",
                "attributes": {
                  "bold": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " run trees ("
              },
              {
                "insert": "paused",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "/"
              },
              {
                "insert": "failed",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ") so the next message does not continue one, attempting to remove the worktrees those runs created (their branches are kept). Owner warnings retain affected checkouts: inspect them ("
              },
              {
                "insert": "lsof",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " when output is still held), resolve the warning, then use "
              },
              {
                "insert": "/workflow abandon <id>",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " on each cancelled run to retry removal. Runs that are actively executing ("
              },
              {
                "insert": "pending",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "/"
              },
              {
                "insert": "running",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ") are never touched -- they may belong to another process entirely. Each cleanup effect still runs if another fails; an incomplete reset tells you to retry and does not promise a fresh next message. The project attachment ("
              },
              {
                "insert": "codebase_id",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": ") is preserved; use "
              },
              {
                "insert": "/detach-project \"<current-project-name>\"",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " to detach it after resolving blockers. Retention follows the checkout ID: a separate checkout can still release after its owner stops. A sub-run without an answering endpoint retains its checkout, even if this reset stops another run with matching host, PID, and user metadata: those fields cannot identify a process incarnation, and the enclosing execution may still be active. Inspect that execution before stopping or abandoning its whole scope; repeated child-only abandonment may still retain the checkout."
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "/help",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "Show all commands"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
